on March 16, 1938, under authority of the Migratory Bird 
Treaty Act of July 3, 1918 (40 Stat. 755):
Regulation Designating as Closed Area Certain Lands and  
Waters Within, Adjacent to, and in the Vicinity of Pea  
Island Migratory Waterfowl Refuge, North Carolina
